{%- comment -%}
  PM — HP hardware configurator wizard (metafield-driven). v3.4.

  v3.4 (Anuj): two close-bugs. (1) On close the pips/checkmarks used to
  vanish a beat AFTER the modal — the old close flipped the `hidden`
  attribute on a setTimeout that raced the opacity transition. Fixed by
  making open/close purely class-driven: opacity + visibility +
  pointer-events all transition together on .is-open, no display/`hidden`
  toggle at all. (2) The floating navy X blended into the site's navy nav
  bar — moved it INTO the white title header (right side) as a circular
  navy-on-white button (fills navy on hover), so it always stands out.

  v3.3 (Anuj): "Configure Your System" is now a large full-width TITLE bar
  across the top of the whole modal (its heading), with the two-column
  media+config row below it. Modal a touch wider (1000px). The qty stepper
  MOVED out of the footer into the body — it renders below the Review list
  ("below Graphics"), so the footer's primary button stays ONE consistent
  full-width size on every step (Next and Add to Cart share identical
  treatment; the button no longer changes size when you reach Review).

  v3.2 (Anuj): the Review step is now the checkout point — Next is REPLACED
  by a qty stepper (− N +) + a terracotta "Add to Cart". Clicking it REUSES
  the PDP's own tested add path: sets #pm-pdp-qty to the chosen quantity,
  then clicks the real [data-pm-pdp-add] (which already holds the resolved
  variant + this wizard's data-pm-add-properties), then closes the modal so
  the cart drawer takes over. No new cart/fetch code. Qty is capped at the
  same data-max-qty the PDP uses, so it can never exceed stock. Only shown
  when a real cart button exists (in stock); otherwise Review just keeps
  Previous. One line item of the configured SKU × N.

  v3.1 (Anuj): bigger + more spacious, and NO dropdowns anywhere — every
  axis renders as selectable cards now (Anuj: dropdowns are boring / less
  obvious; max ~6 values per axis, so a scrollable card list is fine). The
  old "5+ values collapse to a <select>" branch is gone. Modal widened to
  940px, media column 320px, all paddings/cards/fonts scaled up so the
  bigger frame doesn't read empty. The left media panel gained a live
  "Your build" summary (every axis + its current pick; dimmed until
  reached, rust dot on the active step, navy once past) — fills the panel
  and mirrors the reference's running-configuration block. Each step also
  got a "Select your <Axis>" hint line above the cards.

  v3.0 (Anuj): full modal redesign, modeled on the structure of a real BTO
  configurator screenshot (HPE's "Customize Your Product") — but PM colors
  throughout, not HPE's teal/green. Two-column layout: LEFT is a .hpw-media
  panel with the product's actual photo/vendor/title (from data-product-*
  attributes on the root div); RIGHT is the same configurator (.hpw-config
  wraps the existing head/body/foot). Collapses to a single column (image
  strip on top) below 760px.

  v2.3 (Anuj): two more from the v2.2 screenshot — (1) Customize had no
  visible border and went invisible-text-on-hover: the --hpw-* CSS vars
  only resolve inside [data-pm-hpw]'s subtree, and the trigger lives
  outside it once moved next to Add to Cart, so var(--hpw-navy) with no
  fallback was silently invalid — fixed by pointing straight at the global
  --pm-navy-deep token with a hardcoded fallback. (2) No gap above the
  button row: PM's real spacing lives on .pm-pdp__cta:first-of-type
  (20px) / .pm-pdp__cta-row (10px, flex, child-neutralization) — reused
  those classes instead of a bespoke .hpw-cta-row reimplementation, which
  is also just more consistent with the rest of the page.

  v2.2 (Anuj): Customize + Add to Cart now sit SIDE BY SIDE (both moved
  into a shared .hpw-cta-row, Customize left / Add to Cart right) instead
  of stacked. Also: the 4 restructured products (see v2.0 note below)
  were missing real inventory — productSet had created their variants
  with 0 quantity, and pm-instock.liquid deliberately requires a real
  positive tracked quantity (ignores inventoryPolicy CONTINUE on purpose,
  per its own header comment) before it'll render Add to Cart at all —
  so the button was silently absent. Fixed by setting quantity 100 /
  tracked / CONTINUE on every variant across all 4 products (API-side,
  not a template change).

  v2.1 (Anuj): was always-inline in the buy-box — now lives behind a
  "Customize" button inserted right next to the real Add to Cart button
  (found via the existing [data-pm-pdp-add] selector, so this stays fully
  self-contained in this snippet — pm-product-detail.liquid untouched).
  Clicking it opens the SAME wizard card in a centered modal (backdrop,
  Escape/backdrop-click/X to close, basic focus handling). HP.com's own
  BTO customize page has 12+ categories (OS, dual/triple M.2 slots, RAID,
  networking, optical drive, keyboard...) — that's their WebSphere Commerce
  direct-storefront system, which PM has no access to. Hermes only exposes
  Processor/Memory/Storage/Graphics, so that's the ceiling here; the modal
  makes the most of what we actually have, it can't manufacture data we
  don't.

  ARCHITECTURE CHANGE from v1.x: the product's real Shopify variant option
  is now a single hidden "Configuration" axis whose value IS the HP SKU
  (Option1 Value = Variant SKU, always identical by construction — see
  HANDOFF-CONFIGURATOR.md). The wizard's real Processor/Memory/Storage/
  Graphics steps come from the product.metafields.hp_hermes.configurator JSON
  metafield instead of product.options_with_values. Why: Shopify caps a
  product at 3 real options, but some HP lines (Z2 Mini, EliteDesk 8 SFF)
  genuinely vary on 4 independent attributes, and Anuj was explicit that
  splitting/merging axes to fit that cap wasn't acceptable — "we can
  create our own custom solution" instead. This is that solution: the
  wizard resolves a real SKU from the metafield's {axes, configs} data,
  then sets the ONE hidden native <select data-pm-pdp-option="0"> to that
  SKU and dispatches `change`, so the PDP's existing variant-switch JS
  still does all price/image/availability/cart-button sync — untouched.

  metafield shape: { axes: { "Processor": [...], "Memory": [...], ... },
  configs: [ { sku, attributes: { "Processor": "...", ... }, ... }, ... ] }.
  The matrix is SPARSE (not every axis combination is a real HP SKU) —
  liveValues()/repairFrom() filter/snap exactly like v1.x did, just
  matching against `configs[].attributes` instead of Shopify variants.

  v1.7 UI carried forward unchanged: pips (navy done-checks, terracotta
  current step), Previous/Next footer (Next disables, doesn't disappear,
  on the final Review step), price deltas per option (blank until real
  TD SYNNEX pricing lands in Variant Price, then lights up automatically),
  adaptive dropdown-vs-cards per step, no in-wizard "add to cart" (the
  page's own real Add to Cart button is already correct by Review), no
  duplicate "Request a quote" (the PDP already has its own).

  Caller gates rendering (HP + tag B2G + real options). Scoped hpw- styles.
  ES5 only. Param: product (required)
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign _wv = product.selected_or_first_available_variant | default: product.variants.first -%}

<div data-pm-hpw
  data-current-sku="{{ _wv.sku | escape }}"
  data-product-title="{{ product.title | escape }}"
  data-product-vendor="{{ product.vendor | escape }}"
  data-product-image="{{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 700 | escape }}"
  data-product-image-alt="{{ product.featured_image.alt | default: product.title | escape }}">
  {%- if product.metafields.hp_hermes.configurator -%}
    <script type="application/json" data-pm-hpw-config>{{ product.metafields.hp_hermes.configurator.value | json }}</script>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

<style>
  [data-pm-hpw]{--hpw-navy:var(--pm-navy-deep,#0d2340);--hpw-rust:var(--pm-terracotta,#b0410f);--hpw-pale:var(--pm-terracotta-pale,#fdf3ee);--hpw-line:var(--pm-ink-200,#e4e7ec);--hpw-line2:var(--pm-ink-100,#eef0f3);--hpw-mut:var(--pm-ink-400,#667085);--hpw-faint:var(--pm-ink-300,#98a2b3);--hpw-ink:var(--pm-ink-800,#1d2939);--hpw-paper:var(--pm-paper,#f6f4ef);display:block;margin:0 0 12px;color:var(--hpw-navy);font-size:14px;line-height:1.4;font-family:var(--pm-font-body,inherit)}
  [data-pm-hpw] *{box-sizing:border-box}
  [data-pm-hpw] button{font-family:inherit}
  .hpw-card{border:1px solid var(--hpw-line);border-radius:14px;background:#fff;overflow:hidden;box-shadow:var(--pm-shadow-sm,0 1px 2px rgba(16,24,40,.05))}
  /* modal card = a column: a full-width TITLE header on top ("Configure Your
     System", the heading for the whole modal), then a two-column row below
     (product media left / configurator right). Height bounded; the header
     is fixed, the columns row flexes and each column scrolls internally. */
  .hpw-modal .hpw-card{display:flex;flex-direction:column;max-height:min(90vh,820px)}
  .hpw-modal-header{flex:none;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:11px;padding:20px 26px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--hpw-line2)}
  .hpw-modal-header > svg{color:var(--hpw-rust);flex:none;width:24px;height:24px}
  .hpw-modal-title{font-size:23px;font-weight:800;color:var(--hpw-navy);line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-.01em}
  .hpw-cols{flex:1;display:flex;min-height:0}
  .hpw-media{background:var(--hpw-paper);padding:26px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;border-right:1px solid var(--hpw-line2);flex:0 0 320px;overflow-y:auto}
  .hpw-media-img{width:100%;aspect-ratio:1;object-fit:contain;background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--hpw-line2);border-radius:12px;padding:14px}
  .hpw-media-vendor{margin-top:18px;display:inline-flex;align-self:flex-start;background:var(--hpw-pale);color:var(--hpw-rust);font-size:10px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.05em;text-transform:uppercase;padding:4px 10px;border-radius:99px}
  .hpw-media-title{margin-top:9px;font-size:16px;font-weight:700;color:var(--hpw-navy);line-height:1.35}
  /* live "Your build" summary — fills the left panel, updates as you pick,
     mirrors the reference's running configuration block */
  .hpw-build{margin-top:20px;padding-top:18px;border-top:1px solid var(--hpw-line2)}
  .hpw-build-h{font-size:10.5px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--hpw-mut);margin-bottom:10px}
  .hpw-build-list{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0}
  .hpw-build-li{padding:8px 0;border-bottom:1px dashed var(--hpw-line);transition:opacity .14s}
  .hpw-build-li:last-child{border-bottom:0}
  .hpw-build-li.is-pending{opacity:.45}
  .hpw-build-k{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;font-size:10px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--hpw-faint)}
  .hpw-build-k .hpw-build-dot{width:6px;height:6px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--hpw-line);flex:none}
  .hpw-build-li.is-set .hpw-build-dot{background:var(--hpw-navy)}
  .hpw-build-li.is-active .hpw-build-dot{background:var(--hpw-rust);box-shadow:0 0 0 3px var(--hpw-pale)}
  .hpw-build-v{display:block;margin-top:3px;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:650;color:var(--hpw-ink);line-height:1.35}
  @media (max-width:760px){
    .hpw-cols{flex-direction:column}
    .hpw-modal-header{padding:16px 18px}
    .hpw-modal-title{font-size:19px}
    .hpw-media{flex:0 0 auto;flex-direction:row;align-items:center;gap:14px;border-right:0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--hpw-line2);padding:16px;overflow:visible}
    .hpw-media-img{width:64px;height:64px;flex:none;padding:6px}
    .hpw-media-vendor{margin-top:0}
    .hpw-media-title{margin-top:0;font-size:14px}
    .hpw-build{display:none} /* the pips + step title already track progress on mobile */
  }
  .hpw-config{min-width:0;flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;overflow:hidden}
  .hpw-head{flex:none;padding:20px 24px 16px}
  .hpw-pips{display:flex;align-items:center}
  .hpw-pip{flex:0 0 28px;width:28px;height:28px;border-radius:50%;border:2px solid var(--hpw-line);background:#fff;color:var(--hpw-faint);font-size:12px;font-weight:800;display:grid;place-items:center;cursor:pointer;padding:0;transition:all .14s ease}
  .hpw-pip:hover{border-color:var(--hpw-faint)}
  .hpw-pip.is-done{background:var(--hpw-navy);border-color:var(--hpw-navy);color:#fff}
  .hpw-pip.is-now{background:var(--hpw-rust);border-color:var(--hpw-rust);color:#fff;box-shadow:0 0 0 3px var(--hpw-pale)}
  .hpw-pipline{flex:1 1 6px;height:2px;background:var(--hpw-line);margin:0 4px;min-width:6px}
  /* eyebrow + big title (STEP N — small terracotta label / large navy
     category name), matching the reference's clear step labeling instead
     of the old single small "Step N of N · X" line */
  .hpw-stepname{margin-top:18px}
  .hpw-step-eyebrow{display:block;font-size:11.5px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--hpw-rust)}
  .hpw-step-title{display:block;font-size:24px;font-weight:800;color:var(--hpw-navy);margin-top:4px;line-height:1.15}
  .hpw-step-hint{margin:16px 0 12px;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hpw-mut)}
  .hpw-body{flex:1;min-height:0;padding:6px 24px 8px;overflow-y:auto;overscroll-behavior:contain}
  .hpw-list{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:10px;margin:0 0 8px}
  .hpw-list.hpw-cols{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}
  .hpw-opt{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:13px;width:100%;margin:0;padding:16px 16px;background:#fff;border:1.5px solid var(--hpw-line);border-radius:11px;cursor:pointer;text-align:left;transition:border-color .12s,background .12s,box-shadow .12s}
  .hpw-opt:hover{border-color:var(--hpw-faint);background:var(--hpw-paper)}
  .hpw-opt.is-on{border-color:var(--hpw-rust);background:var(--hpw-pale);box-shadow:0 0 0 1px var(--hpw-rust)}
  .hpw-radio{flex:none;width:19px;height:19px;border-radius:50%;border:2px solid var(--hpw-faint);transition:all .12s}
  .hpw-opt.is-on .hpw-radio{border-color:var(--hpw-rust);box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 4px var(--hpw-rust)}
  .hpw-opt-txt{flex:1;min-width:0}
  .hpw-opt-label{display:block;font-size:14px;line-height:1.35;color:var(--hpw-ink);font-weight:600;overflow-wrap:anywhere}
  .hpw-d{display:block;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;color:var(--hpw-mut);margin-top:3px}
  .hpw-d.is-up{color:var(--hpw-rust)}
  .hpw-opt.is-on .hpw-d{color:var(--hpw-rust)}
  .hpw-rev{list-style:none;margin:0 0 6px;padding:0}
  .hpw-rev li{display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:10px;padding:12px 2px;font-size:14px;border-bottom:1px dashed var(--hpw-line2)}
  .hpw-rev li:last-child{border-bottom:0}
  .hpw-rev .hpw-li-k{flex:0 0 116px;color:var(--hpw-faint);font-size:11px;font-weight:800;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.05em}
  .hpw-rev b{font-weight:650;color:var(--hpw-ink);line-height:1.35}
  /* Quantity row — lives in the BODY on the Review step, below the build
     summary (not crammed into the footer), so the footer's primary button
     stays one consistent full-width size across every step. */
  .hpw-qtyrow{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;margin:18px 0 4px;padding:16px;border:1.5px solid var(--hpw-line);border-radius:12px;background:var(--hpw-paper)}
  .hpw-qtyrow-label{font-size:14px;font-weight:700;color:var(--hpw-navy)}
  .hpw-qty{flex:none;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;border:1.5px solid var(--hpw-line);border-radius:10px;overflow:hidden;background:#fff}
  .hpw-qty-btn{width:42px;height:44px;border:0;background:#fff;color:var(--hpw-navy);font-size:20px;font-weight:700;cursor:pointer;line-height:1;transition:background .12s}
  .hpw-qty-btn:hover{background:var(--hpw-paper)}
  .hpw-qty-btn:disabled{opacity:.35;cursor:not-allowed}
  .hpw-qty-val{min-width:44px;text-align:center;font-size:16px;font-weight:700;color:var(--hpw-ink);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
  .hpw-foot{flex:none;padding:16px 24px 20px;border-top:1px solid var(--hpw-line2);background:var(--hpw-paper)}
  .hpw-navrow{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px}
  .hpw-navbtn{border-radius:10px;padding:14px 22px;font-size:14px;font-weight:700;cursor:pointer;white-space:nowrap;transition:filter .12s,border-color .12s,opacity .12s}
  .hpw-prev{flex:none;background:#fff;color:var(--hpw-navy);border:1.5px solid var(--hpw-line)}
  .hpw-prev:hover{border-color:var(--hpw-faint)}
  .hpw-prev[hidden]{display:none}
  /* Next and Add-to-Cart are the SAME button treatment (flex:1, terracotta) —
     the primary action fills the row identically on every step, so it never
     visibly changes size when you reach Review. */
  .hpw-next,.hpw-addcart{flex:1;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:8px;background:var(--hpw-rust);color:#fff;border:0}
  .hpw-next:hover,.hpw-addcart:hover{filter:brightness(.93)}
  .hpw-next[hidden],.hpw-addcart[hidden]{display:none}
  .hpw-addcart svg{flex:none}
  /* trigger sits BESIDE the real Add to Cart button, both wrapped in PM's
     OWN existing .pm-pdp__cta-row (the same class the Datasheet+Email row
     already uses — same gap/flex/child-neutralization mechanics, real PM
     button sizing/padding/radius via .pm-pdp__cta, instead of a bespoke
     reimplementation). .pm-pdp__cta-row's own margin-top is 10px, tuned for
     when it's NOT the first thing in the stack; this row IS first (right
     after Quantity), which normally means the standalone-button 20px rule
     (.pm-pdp__cta:first-of-type) — that selector doesn't match a *row*
     though, so it's set explicitly here.
     Colors: outside [data-pm-hpw]'s subtree once moved via JS, so the
     --hpw-* aliases don't resolve (scoped to that div's descendants) — go
     straight to the global PM tokens with hardcoded fallbacks instead. */
  .hpw-cta-row{margin-top:20px}
  .hpw-trigger{background:#fff;color:var(--pm-navy-deep,#0d2340);border-color:var(--pm-navy-deep,#0d2340);transition:background .12s,color .12s}
  .hpw-trigger:hover{background:var(--pm-navy-deep,#0d2340);color:#fff}
  .hpw-trigger svg{flex:none}
  /* modal: backdrop + centered dialog holding the exact same wizard card —
     wide enough for the two-column media+config layout above */
  /* opacity + visibility + pointer-events ALL transition together, so open
     and close are one coordinated fade — nothing (like the pips) lingers a
     beat after the modal is gone, and no display/`hidden` toggle to race it */
  .hpw-backdrop{position:fixed;inset:0;background:rgba(13,35,64,.55);z-index:9998;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;padding:16px;opacity:0;visibility:hidden;pointer-events:none;transition:opacity .17s ease,visibility .17s ease;overflow-y:auto}
  .hpw-backdrop.is-open{opacity:1;visibility:visible;pointer-events:auto}
  .hpw-modal{position:relative;width:100%;max-width:1000px;margin:auto;transform:translateY(10px);transition:transform .17s ease}
  .hpw-backdrop.is-open .hpw-modal{transform:translateY(0)}
  /* close button lives in the header (right side), on the white bar — a
     circular navy-outlined button that reads clearly against white and
     never blends with the site's navy nav bar the way a floating navy X did */
  .hpw-modal-header .hpw-close{margin-left:auto;flex:none;width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:50%;border:1.5px solid var(--hpw-line);background:#fff;color:var(--hpw-navy);display:grid;place-items:center;cursor:pointer;transition:background .12s,border-color .12s,color .12s}
  .hpw-modal-header .hpw-close:hover{background:var(--hpw-navy);border-color:var(--hpw-navy);color:#fff}
  body.hpw-modal-open{overflow:hidden}
</style>

<script>
(function () {
  'use strict';
  /* the #pm-pdp-variants island renders BELOW this snippet in the buy-box —
     wait for DOM readiness so both JSON islands exist before we init */
  if (document.readyState === 'loading') { document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', init); } else { init(); }
  function init() {
  var root = document.querySelector('[data-pm-hpw]');
  if (!root) return;
  var cfgEl = root.querySelector('[data-pm-hpw-config]');
  var varsEl = document.getElementById('pm-pdp-variants');
  if (!cfgEl || !varsEl) return;

  var CONFIG = null, VARS = [];
  try { CONFIG = JSON.parse(cfgEl.textContent); VARS = JSON.parse(varsEl.textContent); } catch (e) { return; }
  if (!CONFIG || !CONFIG.axes || !CONFIG.configs || !CONFIG.configs.length || !VARS.length) return;

  var AXES = [];
  for (var _k in CONFIG.axes) { if (CONFIG.axes.hasOwnProperty(_k)) AXES.push(_k); }
  var CONFIGS = CONFIG.configs;
  if (!AXES.length) return;

  function esc(s) { return String(s == null ? '' : s).replace(/[&<>"]/g, function (c) { return { '&': '&amp;', '<': '&lt;', '>': '&gt;', '"': '&quot;' }[c]; }); }
  function money(cents) {
    try { return new Intl.NumberFormat(undefined, { style: 'currency', currency: (window.Shopify && Shopify.currency && Shopify.currency.active) || 'USD' }).format(cents / 100); }
    catch (e) { return '$' + (cents / 100).toFixed(2); }
  }

  function configForSku(sku) {
    for (var i = 0; i < CONFIGS.length; i++) { if (CONFIGS[i].sku === sku) return CONFIGS[i]; }
    return null;
  }
  function variantForSku(sku) {
    for (var i = 0; i < VARS.length; i++) { if (VARS[i].sku === sku) return VARS[i]; }
    return null;
  }
  function configFor(selArr) {
    for (var i = 0; i < CONFIGS.length; i++) {
      var c = CONFIGS[i], ok = true;
      for (var k = 0; k < AXES.length; k++) { if (c.attributes[AXES[k]] !== selArr[k]) { ok = false; break; } }
      if (ok) return c;
    }
    return null;
  }

  var N = AXES.length + 1; /* axis steps + Review */
  var step = 0;
  var initialSku = root.getAttribute('data-current-sku');
  var initialConfig = configForSku(initialSku) || CONFIGS[0];
  var sel = AXES.map(function (axisName) { return initialConfig.attributes[axisName]; }); /* preselect current build */

  function currentConfig() { return configFor(sel); }
  function currentVariant() { var c = currentConfig(); return c ? variantForSku(c.sku) : null; }
  /* values of axis i that exist given picks on steps < i */
  function liveValues(i, selArr) {
    var pool = CONFIGS.filter(function (c) {
      for (var k = 0; k < i; k++) {
        if (selArr[k] != null && c.attributes[AXES[k]] !== selArr[k]) return false;
      }
      return true;
    });
    var seen = {}, out = [];
    (CONFIG.axes[AXES[i]] || []).forEach(function (val) {
      if (!seen[val] && pool.some(function (c) { return c.attributes[AXES[i]] === val; })) { seen[val] = 1; out.push(val); }
    });
    return out;
  }
  /* repair later picks in selArr so the combo stays a real config */
  function repairFrom(i, selArr) {
    for (var k = i + 1; k < AXES.length; k++) {
      var live = liveValues(k, selArr);
      if (live.indexOf(selArr[k]) === -1) selArr[k] = live[0] || null;
    }
  }
  /* full repaired-combo price if axis `stepIdx` were set to `val` */
  function priceIf(stepIdx, val) {
    var trial = sel.slice();
    trial[stepIdx] = val;
    repairFrom(stepIdx, trial);
    var c = configFor(trial);
    var v = c ? variantForSku(c.sku) : null;
    return v && typeof v.price === 'number' ? v.price : null;
  }
  /* push the resolved SKU into the ONE hidden native select → PDP sync JS
     does the rest (price/image/availability/cart-button all update) */
  function syncSelects() {
    var c = currentConfig();
    var s = document.querySelector('[data-pm-pdp-option="0"]');
    if (s && c && s.value !== c.sku) {
      s.value = c.sku;
      var ev; try { ev = new Event('change', { bubbles: true }); } catch (e) { ev = document.createEvent('Event'); ev.initEvent('change', true, true); }
      s.dispatchEvent(ev);
    }
    /* Add to Cart should remember the build: stash the picked axes as cart
       line-item properties (pm-add-to-cart.js reads data-pm-add-properties).
       The cart drawer already renders any line's `properties` as a
       "Configured build" accordion (built for the bundle configurator) — this
       just feeds it the same shape, so no cart-side changes were needed. */
    if (addBtn) {
      if (c) {
        var props = {};
        AXES.forEach(function (axisName, i) { if (sel[i] != null) props[axisName] = sel[i]; });
        var v = variantForSku(c.sku);
        if (v && typeof v.price === 'number') props['Configured total'] = money(v.price);
        addBtn.setAttribute('data-pm-add-properties', JSON.stringify(props));
      } else {
        addBtn.removeAttribute('data-pm-add-properties');
      }
    }
  }

  var gear = '<svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"/><path d="M19.4 15a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 .33 1.82l.06.06a2 2 0 1 1-2.83 2.83l-.06-.06a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1.82-.33 1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1 1.51V21a2 2 0 1 1-4 0v-.09A1.65 1.65 0 0 0 9 19.4a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1.82.33l-.06.06a2 2 0 1 1-2.83-2.83l.06-.06a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 .33-1.82 1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1.51-1H3a2 2 0 1 1 0-4h.09A1.65 1.65 0 0 0 4.6 9a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-.33-1.82l-.06-.06a2 2 0 1 1 2.83-2.83l.06.06a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1.82.33H9a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1-1.51V3a2 2 0 1 1 4 0v.09a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1 1.51 1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1.82-.33l.06-.06a2 2 0 1 1 2.83 2.83l-.06.06a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-.33 1.82V9a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1.51 1H21a2 2 0 1 1 0 4h-.09a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1.51 1z"/></svg>';
  var check = '<svg width="10" height="10" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>';
  var xicon = '<svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M18 6 6 18M6 6l12 12"/></svg>';

  var prodTitle = root.getAttribute('data-product-title') || '';
  var prodVendor = root.getAttribute('data-product-vendor') || '';
  var prodImage = root.getAttribute('data-product-image') || '';
  var prodImageAlt = root.getAttribute('data-product-image-alt') || prodTitle;

  var card = document.createElement('div');
  card.className = 'hpw-card';
  card.innerHTML =
    /* full-width TITLE header — the heading for the whole modal; close
       button lives HERE (on the white header), never floating over the
       site's navy nav bar where a navy X would blend in */
    '<div class="hpw-modal-header">' + gear + '<span class="hpw-modal-title">Configure Your System</span>'
    + '<button type="button" class="hpw-close" data-close aria-label="Close">' + xicon + '</button></div>'
    + '<div class="hpw-cols">'
    /* left: real product media — same photo/title/vendor as the PDP */
    + '<div class="hpw-media">'
    + (prodImage ? '<img class="hpw-media-img" src="' + esc(prodImage) + '" alt="' + esc(prodImageAlt) + '" loading="lazy">' : '')
    + (prodVendor ? '<div class="hpw-media-vendor">' + esc(prodVendor) + '</div>' : '')
    + (prodTitle ? '<div class="hpw-media-title">' + esc(prodTitle) + '</div>' : '')
    + '<div class="hpw-build"><div class="hpw-build-h">Your build</div><ul class="hpw-build-list" data-build></ul></div>'
    + '</div>'
    /* right: the interactive configurator (per-step pips/title/body/footer) */
    + '<div class="hpw-config">'
    + '<div class="hpw-head">'
    + '<div class="hpw-pips" data-pips></div>'
    + '<div class="hpw-stepname" data-stepname></div>'
    + '</div>'
    + '<div class="hpw-body" data-body></div>'
    + '<div class="hpw-foot">'
    + '<div class="hpw-navrow">'
    + '<button type="button" class="hpw-navbtn hpw-prev" data-prev hidden>&larr; Previous</button>'
    + '<button type="button" class="hpw-navbtn hpw-next" data-next>Next &rarr;</button>'
    + '<button type="button" class="hpw-navbtn hpw-addcart" data-addcart hidden>Add to Cart</button>'
    + '</div>'
    + '</div>'
    + '</div>'
    + '</div>';

  /* modal: backdrop + dialog wrapping the same card — opened via a
     "Customize" trigger inserted right next to the real Add to Cart
     button (found by its existing stable [data-pm-pdp-add] selector, so
     this whole feature stays self-contained in this one snippet — no
     changes needed to pm-product-detail.liquid). */
  var backdrop = document.createElement('div');
  backdrop.className = 'hpw-backdrop';
  backdrop.setAttribute('role', 'dialog');
  backdrop.setAttribute('aria-modal', 'true');
  backdrop.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Configure your system');
  var modal = document.createElement('div');
  modal.className = 'hpw-modal';
  modal.appendChild(card);
  backdrop.appendChild(modal);
  root.appendChild(backdrop);
  var closeBtn = card.querySelector('[data-close]'); /* now inside the header */

  var addBtn = document.querySelector('[data-pm-pdp-add]');
  var trigger = document.createElement('button');
  trigger.type = 'button';
  /* pm-pdp__cta = PM's real button base (sizing/padding/radius/font);
     hpw-trigger = just the navy color override on top of it */
  trigger.className = 'pm-pdp__cta hpw-trigger';
  trigger.innerHTML = gear + 'Customize';
  if (addBtn && addBtn.parentNode) {
    /* Customize sits BESIDE Add to Cart, on the left — wrap both in PM's
       own .pm-pdp__cta-row (Datasheet+Email already uses this exact
       pattern), inserted at Add to Cart's original spot, Add to Cart
       moved into it. addBtn already carries .pm-pdp__cta from the Liquid
       markup, so .pm-pdp__cta-row's child-neutralization rule picks it up
       automatically — nothing to change on addBtn itself. */
    var ctaRow = document.createElement('div');
    ctaRow.className = 'pm-pdp__cta-row hpw-cta-row';
    addBtn.parentNode.insertBefore(ctaRow, addBtn);
    ctaRow.appendChild(trigger);
    ctaRow.appendChild(addBtn);
  } else {
    root.parentNode.insertBefore(trigger, root); /* defensive fallback if the cart button ever isn't there yet */
  }

  var lastFocused = null;
  /* Open/close is driven PURELY by the is-open class (opacity + visibility +
     pointer-events all transition together — see CSS). No display/`hidden`
     toggling: the old setTimeout that flipped `hidden` after the fade raced
     the transition and left the pips/checkmarks painting a beat AFTER the
     modal had already gone. The backdrop just stays in the DOM, invisible
     and non-interactive (visibility:hidden + pointer-events:none) until
     is-open flips everything on/off in one coordinated transition. */
  function openModal() {
    lastFocused = document.activeElement;
    backdrop.classList.add('is-open');
    document.body.classList.add('hpw-modal-open');
    if (closeBtn) closeBtn.focus();
    document.addEventListener('keydown', onKeydown);
  }
  function closeModal() {
    backdrop.classList.remove('is-open');
    document.body.classList.remove('hpw-modal-open');
    document.removeEventListener('keydown', onKeydown);
    if (lastFocused && lastFocused.focus) lastFocused.focus();
  }
  function onKeydown(e) { if (e.key === 'Escape') closeModal(); }

  trigger.addEventListener('click', openModal);
  closeBtn.addEventListener('click', closeModal);
  backdrop.addEventListener('click', function (e) { if (e.target === backdrop) closeModal(); });

  var pipsEl = card.querySelector('[data-pips]'), nameEl = card.querySelector('[data-stepname]'),
      bodyEl = card.querySelector('[data-body]'), prevEl = card.querySelector('[data-prev]'),
      nextEl = card.querySelector('[data-next]'), buildEl = card.querySelector('[data-build]'),
      addCartEl = card.querySelector('[data-addcart]');
  var cartIcon = '<svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.25" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="9" cy="21" r="1"/><circle cx="20" cy="21" r="1"/><path d="M1 1h4l2.68 13.39a2 2 0 0 0 2 1.61h9.72a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.61L23 6H6"/></svg>';
  addCartEl.innerHTML = cartIcon + 'Add to Cart';

  /* qty for the review-step Add to Cart. The qty control lives in the BODY
     (rendered below the build summary on the review step), NOT the footer.
     The actual add REUSES the PDP's own tested handler: we set the PDP qty
     input then click the real [data-pm-pdp-add] button (which already
     carries the resolved variant + data-pm-add-properties this wizard set).
     No new cart/fetch code — one line item of the configured SKU, qty N. */
  var qty = 1;
  function maxQty() {
    var m = addBtn ? parseInt(addBtn.getAttribute('data-max-qty'), 10) : NaN;
    return (!isNaN(m) && m > 0) ? m : 999;
  }
  function qtyRowHtml() {
    /* only shown on review, and only when there's a real cart button */
    if (!addBtn) return '';
    var max = maxQty();
    return '<div class="hpw-qtyrow">'
      + '<span class="hpw-qtyrow-label">Quantity</span>'
      + '<div class="hpw-qty" data-qty>'
      + '<button type="button" class="hpw-qty-btn" data-qty-dec aria-label="Decrease quantity"' + (qty <= 1 ? ' disabled' : '') + '>&minus;</button>'
      + '<span class="hpw-qty-val" data-qty-val aria-live="polite">' + qty + '</span>'
      + '<button type="button" class="hpw-qty-btn" data-qty-inc aria-label="Increase quantity"' + (qty >= max ? ' disabled' : '') + '>+</button>'
      + '</div></div>';
  }
  function updateQtyUi() {
    var vEl = bodyEl.querySelector('[data-qty-val]'), dEl = bodyEl.querySelector('[data-qty-dec]'), iEl = bodyEl.querySelector('[data-qty-inc]');
    if (vEl) vEl.textContent = qty;
    if (dEl) dEl.disabled = qty <= 1;
    if (iEl) iEl.disabled = qty >= maxQty();
  }
  /* the PDP already has its own always-visible Request a Quote button —
     the wizard doesn't need a second one duplicating it on the review step */

  /* left-panel live "Your build" summary — every axis + its current pick,
     dimmed until reached, rust dot on the step you're on, navy once past.
     Values are always present (the wizard preselects the current variant),
     so this is a real running config, not placeholders. */
  function renderBuild() {
    if (!buildEl) return;
    var h = '', reviewing = (step === N - 1);
    AXES.forEach(function (axisName, i) {
      var state = reviewing || i < step ? 'is-set' : (i === step ? 'is-active is-set' : 'is-pending');
      h += '<li class="hpw-build-li ' + state + '">'
        + '<span class="hpw-build-k"><span class="hpw-build-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>' + esc(axisName) + '</span>'
        + '<span class="hpw-build-v">' + esc(sel[i] == null ? '—' : sel[i]) + '</span>'
        + '</li>';
    });
    buildEl.innerHTML = h;
  }

  function renderPips() {
    var h = '', i;
    for (i = 0; i < N; i++) {
      if (i > 0) h += '<span class="hpw-pipline" aria-hidden="true"></span>';
      var cls = i < step ? ' is-done' : (i === step ? ' is-now' : '');
      var lbl = i < AXES.length ? AXES[i] : 'Review';
      h += '<button type="button" class="hpw-pip' + cls + '" data-pip="' + i + '" aria-label="Step ' + (i + 1) + ': ' + esc(lbl) + '"' + (i === step ? ' aria-current="step"' : '') + '>'
        + (i < step ? check : (i + 1)) + '</button>';
    }
    pipsEl.innerHTML = h;
  }

  /* Previous/Next on option steps. On the final Review step, Next is
     REPLACED by a qty stepper + terracotta "Add to Cart" (only when a real
     PDP cart button exists — i.e. the product is in stock; otherwise nothing
     to add, leave just Previous). Previous stays throughout so you can go
     back and change the build. */
  function renderNav() {
    var last = step === N - 1;
    prevEl.hidden = step === 0;
    /* on Review, Next is replaced by Add to Cart (same size/treatment, so
       the primary button never visibly changes). Add to Cart only when a
       real PDP cart button exists (in stock). */
    nextEl.hidden = last;
    addCartEl.hidden = !(last && !!addBtn);
  }

  function renderStep() {
    var h = '';
    if (step === N - 1) {
      nameEl.innerHTML = '<span class="hpw-step-eyebrow">Step ' + N + ' of ' + N + '</span><span class="hpw-step-title">Review your build</span>';
      h = '<ul class="hpw-rev">';
      AXES.forEach(function (axisName, i) {
        h += '<li><span class="hpw-li-k">' + esc(axisName) + '</span><b>' + esc(sel[i] == null ? '—' : sel[i]) + '</b></li>';
      });
      h += '</ul>';
      h += qtyRowHtml(); /* qty control sits here in the body, below the build */
    } else {
      var axisName = AXES[step];
      nameEl.innerHTML = '<span class="hpw-step-eyebrow">Step ' + (step + 1) + ' of ' + N + '</span><span class="hpw-step-title">' + esc(axisName) + '</span>';
      var live = liveValues(step, sel);
      var curPrice = null;
      var curVariant = currentVariant();
      if (curVariant && typeof curVariant.price === 'number') curPrice = curVariant.price;
      function deltaOf(val) {
        if (curPrice == null || sel[step] === val) return null;
        var p = priceIf(step, val);
        if (p == null) return null;
        var diff = p - curPrice;
        return diff === 0 ? null : diff;
      }
      /* ALWAYS selectable cards now — no dropdowns (Anuj: they're boring /
         less obvious). Max real value-count per axis is ~6, so a scrollable
         card list is fine. Two columns only when every value is short
         (Memory-style "1 x 16 GB"); long spec strings get full-width rows. */
      h = '<div class="hpw-step-hint">Select your ' + esc(axisName) + '</div>';
      var cols = live.every(function (v) { return v.length <= 16; });
      h += '<div class="hpw-list' + (cols ? ' hpw-cols' : '') + '">';
      live.forEach(function (val) {
        var on = sel[step] === val;
        var diff = deltaOf(val), d = '';
        if (diff != null) d = '<span class="hpw-d' + (diff > 0 ? ' is-up' : '') + '">' + (diff > 0 ? '+' : '&minus;') + money(Math.abs(diff)) + '</span>';
        h += '<button type="button" class="hpw-opt' + (on ? ' is-on' : '') + '" data-val="' + esc(val) + '" aria-pressed="' + (on ? 'true' : 'false') + '">'
          + '<span class="hpw-radio" aria-hidden="true"></span>'
          + '<span class="hpw-opt-txt"><span class="hpw-opt-label">' + esc(val) + '</span>' + d + '</span>'
          + '</button>';
      });
      h += '</div>';
    }
    bodyEl.innerHTML = h;
    bodyEl.scrollTop = 0;
    renderNav();
  }

  function paint() { renderPips(); renderStep(); renderBuild(); }
  paint();
  syncSelects(); /* align page with the preselected combo */

  root.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
    var pip = e.target.closest('[data-pip]');
    if (pip) { step = parseInt(pip.getAttribute('data-pip'), 10) || 0; paint(); return; }

    var opt = e.target.closest('[data-val]');
    if (opt && step < AXES.length) {
      sel[step] = opt.getAttribute('data-val');
      repairFrom(step, sel);
      syncSelects();
      renderStep();   /* refresh the highlighted pick in the right panel */
      renderBuild();  /* and the running summary in the left panel */
      return;
    }

    if (e.target.closest('[data-prev]')) { if (step > 0) { step--; paint(); } return; }

    if (e.target.closest('[data-next]')) { if (step < N - 1) { step++; paint(); } return; }

    if (e.target.closest('[data-qty-dec]')) { if (qty > 1) { qty--; updateQtyUi(); } return; }
    if (e.target.closest('[data-qty-inc]')) { if (qty < maxQty()) { qty++; updateQtyUi(); } return; }

    if (e.target.closest('[data-addcart]')) {
      if (!addBtn) return;
      /* make sure the hidden native select really is on the resolved SKU
         (it is, from syncSelects on each pick — belt-and-suspenders), push
         the chosen qty into the PDP's own qty input, then trigger the REAL
         Add to Cart button. It reads #pm-pdp-qty + data-pm-add-properties
         (set by syncSelects) and does the tested /cart/add.js flow. */
      syncSelects();
      var pdpQty = document.getElementById('pm-pdp-qty');
      if (pdpQty) { pdpQty.value = qty; try { pdpQty.dispatchEvent(new Event('change', { bubbles: true })); } catch (e2) {} }
      addBtn.click();
      closeModal(); /* let the cart drawer (opened on pm:cart-changed) take over */
      return;
    }
  });
  }
})();
</script>
